  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Water, sanitation and hygiene dissemination grants: promoting effluent pasteurization in faecal sludge treatment to contribute to the preventionof cholera outbreaks</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project focuses on disseminating results and promoting uptake of solar pasteurization for cholera prevention and control. In South Sudan, engagement with national stakeholders is planned for Q3&#x2013;Q4 2025, including participation in a water, sanitation, and hygiene (WASH) Cluster meeting and discussions with partners such as MSF and the Ministry of Health to consider adaptation pathways and gather feedback. Over the same period, tailored communication products&#x2014;such as a short video, a technical brief, and a case study&#x2014;are to be produced and shared through sector platforms like Sanihub and professional networks such as LinkedIn. In addition, project findings will be presented in two academic seminars hosted by the University of Cape Town and the University of KwaZulu-Natal.</narrative>
  </description>
